<title>CANADA: Inco in tentative deal with Thompson union.</title>
<headline>Inco in tentative deal with Thompson union.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inco Ltd said on Friday it had reached a tentative three-year labor agreement with union representatives at its Thompson, Manitoba nickel facility.</p>
<p>The deal, to face a ratification vote by members of the United Steelworkers of America local on Sunday, September 29, would end a lock-out imposed by Inco on September 15.</p>
<p>Results of the vote are expected to be known at about 9:00 p.m. central time Sunday (0200 GMT Monday), Inco spokesman Mark Tessier told Reuters.</p>
</text>
